      "id": "bug-020",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-21T00:00:00.000Z",
      "error_message": "Tried reverting to input context [] which is not defined. Current context [TEXT_INPUT] — inputs dead after closing UI",
      "file": "xml/gui/WMEditorDialog.xml, WMMainDialog.xml, WMStepDialog.xml, WMADSettingsDialog.xml, TextInputDialog.xml, WMModeSelectDialog.xml",
      "root_cause": "All dialogs used custom inputContext names (e.g. DIALOG_WMEditorDialog) not registered with FS25 InputBinding. When TextInputElement gained focus it pushed TEXT_INPUT with previous context = '' (empty string). On focus-leave it tried revertContext to '' which is undefined, corrupting the input stack so no inputs worked after dialog close.",
      "fix": "Changed inputContext attribute to 'MENU' in all 6 dialog XML files. MENU is a standard registered FS25 context, so TextInputElement can revert to it cleanly.",
      "tags": ["input-context", "text-input", "dialog", "xml", "input-freeze"],
      "related_bugs": ["bug-019"],
      "occurrences": 1,
      "last_seen": "2026-05-21T00:00:00.000Z"
